# Build output of paper/build_paper_artifacts.py.
#
# Not committed, on purpose. These files are a pure function of the receipts,
# the claim chain and the charter -- all of which ARE committed -- so carrying
# them here would mean a second copy that can silently disagree with the first.
# The generator is the artifact; its output is regenerated by running it.
#
# The reproducibility manifest pins its INPUTS by sha256, which is what lets a
# replicator confirm they rebuilt from the same evidence. It is written with LF
# on every platform for that reason -- see _write_lf.
paper/generated/
